# Feed video (Bluesky-standard) — Phase 0

## Freeze (do not violate)

The **Scenes dual-player** experiment is frozen. Do **not**:

- Patch `ScenesViewer` / `ScenesScreen` for dual-player handoff races (poster shutter, InteractionManager tricks)
- Mount a second `react-native-video` / ExoPlayer **while the feed TextureView is still alive**
- Re-introduce Stories 24 preview `<Video>` while a feed postcard can own the slot

Phase 3 immersive Scenes is allowed **only** after the feed player is torn down (`setFeedTextureMountAllowed(false)`), with **one** active Scenes Video + poster-only inactive pages.

Work order: **Phase 1** (single-player feed) → **Phase 2** (same-player fullscreen) → **Phase 3** (immersive Scenes, optional). Do not start a later phase until the earlier phase’s acceptance checks pass on device (Oppo/ColorOS).

Reference: Bluesky `social-app` — one active `BlueskyVideoView`, native `VisibilityView`, fullscreen via same player `enterFullscreen()` — not a second JS player.

## Acceptance criteria (must meet before calling feed video “done”)

### A. Single surface (always)

- [ ] At most **one** audible TextureView / ExoPlayer exists in the feed viewport
- [ ] Non-active video posts show **poster Image only** (no paused TextureView left mounted)
- [ ] Stories 24 rail thumbs are **Image-only** whenever the feed video slot can be active
- [ ] No feed surface rebinds into a top-left mini thumb when opening or closing fullscreen

### B. Autoplay

- [ ] The most-visible video postcard autoplays (muted per global mute)
- [ ] Scrolling away pauses/destroys the previous player; the new active card starts (or shows poster until ready)
- [ ] On Android, active-video selection updates on **scroll settle**, not every viewability tick (avoid ExoPlayer create/destroy jank)
- [ ] App background → pause; foreground → resume the same active card if still visible
- [ ] User preference / global mute is respected across cards

### C. Fullscreen (same player — Phase 2)

- [ ] Tap / “View in scenes” expands **the same** feed player (no second ExoPlayer, no black 2–4s gap)
- [ ] Audio and picture continue without a seek jump (or seek only to the paused handoff time intentionally)
- [ ] Dismiss fullscreen returns to the feed card with the same clip still the active slot
- [ ] No corner-thumb steal / surface swap on enter or exit

### D. Return to feed

- [ ] After fullscreen dismiss, the postcard shows the playing (or correctly paused) frame, not a black hole
- [ ] Viewability cannot immediately steal the slot from the returning card for a short grace window
- [ ] Mute state matches what the user left fullscreen with (or global mute)

