## Phase 4 decision (2026-09-28)

**Recommendation: keep `react-native-video` ^6.19. Keep adopting Bluesky’s rules, not their package.**

| Factor | `@bsky.app/video` / bluesky-video | Our stack (`react-native-video`) |
|--------|-----------------------------------|----------------------------------|
| Architecture | Native `BlueskyVideoView` + `enterFullscreen()` → `FullscreenActivity` | JS Video + `armFeedExpand` same-player morph (Phase 2) |
| Bare RN fit | Expo module (`peer: expo`); needs expo-modules host / autolinking / native rebuild | Already shipping on bare RN 0.85 |
| Docs / support | Usage TODO; Bluesky-app-first support | Mature; we own patches |
| ColorOS | Bluesky still hits Android fullscreen black/audio bugs | Dual-player was our failure mode; Phase 1–2 remove that |
| Cost to switch | Large epic: Expo modules wiring, replace FeedPostMedia + cache, Android `FullscreenActivity`, iOS rebuild | Already done |

**When to revisit:** only if Oppo still fails Phase 1–2 acceptance **after** a clean device verify (single surface + CTA expand + return), and a spike proves `enterFullscreen` is stable on ColorOS. Do **not** install `@bsky.app/video` as a speculative fix.

## When implementing Phase 1+

- Prefer changing `feedActiveVideoNative` + `FeedPostMedia.native.tsx` + Stories 24 thumbs
- Phase 2: **Bluesky enterFullscreen** — tap = `presentFullscreenPlayer()` (RNV), matching `videoRef.enterFullscreen(true)` in Bluesky’s `VideoEmbedInnerNative`. **Not** a JS scale morph inside FlashList. **Mute = mute control only**
- Phase A start latency: warm **imminent** active URI (not only siblings); `prioritizeFirst` Range prebuffer; `bufferForPlaybackMs: 100`; keep elevated poster until `onReadyForDisplay`; `__DEV__` logs `[feed-video] firstFrame Nms`
- Phase B: **do not destroy ExoPlayer on every scroll** — pause+mute and keep TextureView; tear down only after ~160px leave; same-card settle = resume (no remount)
- Phase 3 immersive Scenes navigate is **deferred** on ColorOS (black surface); do not re-enable dual-mount
- Phase 4: stay on `react-native-video` unless ColorOS spike overturns the decision above
- Verify on a real Android device (ColorOS), not only iOS simulator
